# Celestial Colonnade is played on turn 1, when it enters tapped, and sits there as a land. On turn 9 Bot1 has five
# other mana sources, animates it, and attacks: layer 4 makes it a creature without taking the land away, layer 7b
# gives it 4/4, and layer 6 gives it flying and vigilance, so Bot2's ground Elvish Spirit Guide is offered no block and the
# Colonnade never taps to attack. The trailing wait on turn 10 shows the effect ending in the cleanup step: it is a
# plain Land again, with no power to read.
#
# Turn 9 rather than turn 6 because the Colonnade itself is not tapped for mana here — spending it would leave it
# tapped and unable to attack, which is the interesting half of the card.

